## Correction to the prior test battery

I had "make sure it lands well with the board" → `unclassified`. That contradicts C.1: it names a third-party reaction after delivery, which is the definition of an objective. It routes to **`objective`**, and the contract is `ready`, not `ready_with_warnings`.

I was wrong there, and the error is instructive — I reached for `unclassified` for something that had a perfectly good typed home. That is precisely the archival reflex you're worried about, and it showed up in my own test expectations rather than in the rules.

