## Revised D3–D4, plus new D.7

```
D.3 SLOT CLASSES.

    TRANSCRIPTION SLOTS — verbatim, double-quoted:
      objective, constraints, required_checks, invalidation,
      unclassified, input.imitate, input.conform, both sides of
      every conflicts entry

      No paraphrase, no tidying, no compression. You normalise
      PLACEMENT, not LANGUAGE. Fidelity outranks legibility.

    DERIVED SLOTS — canonical form, authored by you:
      action, accepted when, subordinate, role labels, status

D.4 COMPETING PHRASINGS. In transcription slots, where the same
    requirement is stated two non-identical ways, both are preserved.
    Choosing the better phrasing is silent drift.

    In derived slots, competing phrasings are traced together:
      action: reconcile renewals
              ← "where we are on the renewals" / "renewal status"

D.7 DERIVATION DISCIPLINE. A derived field is valid only if it adds
    no requirement absent from the input and drops none present in
    it. Change of form is permitted; change of extension is not.

    Every derived field carries its source inline:

      action: summarise renewal status
              ← "get the board something showing where we are on
                 the renewals"

    If you cannot quote a source span, you have invented the field.
    Emit [UNSPECIFIED] instead.
```

